 {"edgeAttributes":[{"po":46,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9521656\">pubmed:9521656</a> These data suggest that the physiological role of UCH is to hydrolyze small adducts of ubiquitin and to generate free monomeric ubiquitin from ubiquitin proproteins, but not to deubiquitinate ubiquitin-protein conjugates or disassemble polyubiquitin chains"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"42.0","d":"double"}, {"po":46,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:9521656"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":46,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":46,"n":"name","v":"UCHL1 (up-regulates quantity) UBC"}, {"po":46,"n":"mechanism","v":["cleavage"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/11583623\">pubmed:11583623</a> Here we report that a serine protease called htra2/omi is released from mitochondria and inhibits the function of xiap by direct binding in a similar way to diablo."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"99.3333333333333","d":"double"}, {"po":41,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:11583623"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":41,"n":"annotator","v":["gcesareni"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":41,"n":"name","v":"HTRA2 (down-regulates) XIAP"}, {"po":41,"n":"mechanism","v":["binding"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20479780\">pubmed:20479780</a> The genetic causes of PD seem to participate in con­ verging pathways to pathogenesis, but it is unclear whether all or only some of these pathways need to be activated for lewy body deposition and neuronal death to occur."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"88.33333333333331","d":"double"}, {"po":27,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000938"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:20479780"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":27,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":27,"n":"name","v":"Lewy_body_formation (up-regulates) Apoptosis"}, {"po":27,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/16000336\">pubmed:16000336</a> The increased concentration of neuronal alpha-synuclein and pigment in normal A9 neurons may already predispose these neurons to precipitate alpha-synuclein around pigment-associated lipid under oxidative conditions."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"128.0","d":"double"}, {"po":50,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:16000336"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":50,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":50,"n":"name","v":"ROS (up-regulates quantity) SNCA"}, {"po":50,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15525720\">pubmed:15525720</a> Mutations in the gene encoding DJ-1 have also been linked to familial Parkinsons disease. Other studies have suggested that DJ-1 protects cells from oxidative damage, and mutations in DJ-1 may therefore contribute to in- creased levels of oxidative stress."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"85.0","d":"double"}, {"po":23,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:15525720"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":23,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":23,"n":"name","v":"DNAJC14 (down-regulates) ROS"}, {"po":23,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12666095\">pubmed:12666095</a> Furthermore, mutant isoforms of alpha-synuclein more readily oligomerize, and it has been suggested that its tendency to aggregate into misfolded structures may confer toxic properties to the protein."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"86.0","d":"double"}, {"po":30,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:12666095"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":30,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":30,"n":"name","v":"SNCA (up-regulates) ER stress"}, {"po":30,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12666095\">pubmed:12666095</a> A key observation linking alpha-synuclein to PD was the demonstration that it is one of the principal components of Lewy bodies. Furthermore, mutant isoforms of alpha-synuclein more readily oligomerize, and it has been suggested that its tendency to aggregate into misfolded structures may confer toxic properties to the protein. "],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"161.33333333333331","d":"double"}, {"po":25,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:12666095"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"direct","v":"false","d":"boolean"}, {"po":25,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":25,"n":"name","v":"SNCA (up-regulates) Lewy_body_formation"}, {"po":25,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15657060\">pubmed:15657060</a>  Following autoprocessing in the apoptosome, caspase-9 cleaves and activates caspase-3.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9390557\">pubmed:9390557</a> Activated caspase-9  in turn cleaves and activates caspase-3. Mutation of the active site of caspase-9 attenuated the activation of caspase-3 and cellular apoptotic response in vivo, indicating that caspase-9 is the most upstream member of the apoptotic protease cascade."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"160.33333333333331","d":"double"}, {"po":43,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"cell_data","v":["","BTO:0000567"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:9390557","pubmed:15657060"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":43,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":43,"n":"name","v":"CASP9 (up-regulates activity) CASP3"}, {"po":43,"n":"mechanism","v":["cleavage"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/26161729\">pubmed:26161729</a> Mechanism of phospho-ubiquitin-induced PARKIN activation|PhosphoUb binding leads to straightening of a helix in the RING1 domain, and the resulting conformational changes release the Ubl domain from the PARKIN core; this activates PARKIN|Our results show that PINK1-dependent phosphorylation of both parkin and ubiquitin is sufficient for full activation of parkin E3 activity. These findings demonstrate that phosphorylated ubiquitin is a parkin activator. "],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"65.0","d":"double"}, {"po":13,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000938"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:26161729"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":13,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":13,"n":"name","v":"UBC (up-regulates activity) PRKN"}, {"po":13,"n":"mechanism","v":["binding"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/12666095\">pubmed:12666095</a> Parkin is a protein of 465 amino acids, and its structure includes a ubiquitin homologous domain in its N terminus and two RING finger domains in its C terminus. Molecular studies have determined that parkin is an E3 ubiquitin ligase function, implicating parkin in the ubiquitin-proteasome system, and raising the possibility that mutations in the gene lead to loss or diminished function. Three substrates for the ubiquitin-ligase function of parkin have been identified to date.1. A 22kDa glycosolated form of alpha-synuclei|2. Parkin-associated endothelin receptor-like receptor (Pael-R)."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"149.33333333333331","d":"double"}, {"po":15,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000938"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:12666095"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":15,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":15,"n":"name","v":"PRKN (down-regulates quantity by destabilization) SNCA"}, {"po":15,"n":"mechanism","v":["ubiquitination"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/9390557\">pubmed:9390557</a> Caspase-9 and apaf-1 bind to each other via their respective nh2-terminal ced-3 homologous domains in the presence of cytochrome c and datp, an event that leads to caspase-9 activation."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"143.3333333333333","d":"double"}, {"po":39,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000567"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:9390557"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":39,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":39,"n":"name","v":"CYCS (up-regulates activity) CASP9"}, {"po":39,"n":"mechanism","v":["binding"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/17906618\">pubmed:17906618</a> Htra2 is phosphorylated on activation of the p38 pathway, occurring in a pink1-dependent mannerwe suggest that pink1-dependent phosphorylation of htra2 might modulate its proteolytic activity, thereby contributing to an increased resistance of cells to mitochondrial stress."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"61.33333333333334","d":"double"}, {"po":32,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:17906618"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":32,"n":"annotator","v":["gcesareni"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"residue","v":["Ser142"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"sequence","v":["VPSPPPAsPRSQYNF"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":32,"n":"name","v":"PINK1 (up-regulates) HTRA2"}, {"po":32,"n":"mechanism","v":["phosphorylation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/24784582\">pubmed:24784582</a> Ubiquitin is phosphorylated by PINK1 to activate parkin|PINK1 phosphorylated ubiquitin at Ser65 both in vitro and in cells"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"16.0","d":"double"}, {"po":31,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000938"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:24784582"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":31,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"residue","v":["Ser65"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"sequence","v":["DYNIQKEsTLHLVLR"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":31,"n":"name","v":"PINK1 (up-regulates activity) UBC"}, {"po":31,"n":"mechanism","v":["phosphorylation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/22724072\">pubmed:22724072</a> PINK1 is activated by mitochondrial membrane potential depolarization and stimulates Parkin E3 ligase activity by phosphorylating Serine 65"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"69.33333333333334","d":"double"}, {"po":12,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000007"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:22724072"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":12,"n":"annotator","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"residue","v":["Ser65"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"sequence","v":["NCDLDQQsIVHIVQR"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":12,"n":"name","v":"PINK1 (up-regulates activity) PRKN"}, {"po":12,"n":"mechanism","v":["phosphorylation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/22724072\">pubmed:22724072</a> We show that human pink1 is specifically activated by mitochondrial membrane potential (??m) depolarization, enabling it to phosphorylate parkin at ser(65). We further show that phosphorylation of parkin at ser(65) leads to marked activation of its e3 ligase activity that is prevented by mutation of ser(65) or inactivation of pink1."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"69.33333333333334","d":"double"}, {"po":7,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"cell_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:22724072"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":7,"n":"annotator","v":["llicata"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"residue","v":["Ser65"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"sequence","v":["NCDLDQQsIVHIVQR"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":7,"n":"name","v":"PINK1 (up-regulates) PRKN"}, {"po":7,"n":"mechanism","v":["phosphorylation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20012177\">pubmed:20012177</a> There is a strong cyto-protective role of PINK1 in maintaining mitochondrial homeostasis via different mechanisms. Overexpression of wild-type PINK1 in SH-SY5Y neuroblastoma cells stabilizes respiring mitochondrial networks through various mechanisms that include maintaining mitochondrial membrane potential, reducing basal and neurotoxin-induced ROS, suppression of cytochrome c release, reversal of toxin-induced fission, and suppression of autophagy"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"61.33333333333334","d":"double"}, {"po":5,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000938"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:20012177"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":5,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"residue","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"sequence","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":5,"n":"name","v":"PINK1 (down-regulates quantity) CYCS"}, {"po":5,"n":"mechanism","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/20022946\">pubmed:20022946</a> We have found that in HEK293 cells and 3T3-L1 adipocytes, insulin promotes both raptor- and rictor-associated mTOR Ser(P)-2481 in a wortmannin-sensitive manner. Thus, insulin signals via PI3K to promote both mTORC1- and mTORC2-associated mTOR Ser-2481 autophosphorylation.","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10702316\">pubmed:10702316</a>  We report here the identification of a FRAP autophosphorylation site. This site, Ser-2481, is located in a hydrophobic region near the conserved carboxyl-terminal FRAP tail. We demonstrate that the COOH-terminal tail is required for FRAP kinase activity and for signaling to the translational regulator p70(s6k) (ribosomal subunit S6 kinase)."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"0.0","d":"double"}, {"po":40,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"cell_data","v":["BTO:0000782","BTO:0000944"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:10702316","pubmed:20022946"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":40,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"residue","v":["Ser2481"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"sequence","v":["TVPESIHsFIGDGLV"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":40,"n":"name","v":"MTOR (up-regulates activity) MTOR"}, {"po":40,"n":"mechanism","v":["phosphorylation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/15718470\">pubmed:15718470</a>  The rictor-mtor complex directly phosphorylated akt/pkb on ser473 in vitro and facilitated thr308 phosphorylation by pdk1","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/21157483\">pubmed:21157483</a>  Mammalian TOR complex 1 (mTORC1) and mTORC2 exert their actions by regulating other important kinases, such as S6 kinase (S6K) and Akt.Recent findings have revealed novel important roles for mTORC2 in the phosphorylation of AGC kinase family members. mTORC2 phosphorylates and activates Akt, SGK, and PKC, which regulate cell survival, cell cycle progression and anabolism","<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/21592956\">pubmed:21592956</a> Protein kinase B (PKB, Akt) is a Ser/Thr kinase involved in the regulation of cell survival, proliferation, and metabolism and is activated by dual phosphorylation on Thr(308) in the activation loop and Ser(473) in the hydrophobic motif. It plays a contributory role to platelet function, although little is known about its regulation. In this study, we investigated the role of the mammalian target of rapamycin complex (mTORC)-2 in Akt regulation using the recently identified small molecule ATP competitive mTOR inhibitors PP242 and Torin1."],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"108.0","d":"double"}, {"po":34,"n":"notes","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"cell_data","v":["","BTO:0000182","BTO:0000018","BTO:0000132"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"citation","v":["pubmed:21592956","pubmed:21157483","pubmed:15718470"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"tissue_data","v":[""],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"direct","v":"true","d":"boolean"}, {"po":34,"n":"annotator","v":["lperfetto"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"residue","v":["Ser473"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"sequence","v":["RPHFPQFsYSASGTA"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":34,"n":"name","v":"MTOR (up-regulates activity) AKT1"}, {"po":34,"n":"mechanism","v":["phosphorylation"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":49,"n":"sentence","v":["<a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://identifiers.org/pubmed/10579725\">pubmed:10579725</a> P53 can inhibit the survival function of integrins by inducing the caspase-dependent cleavage and inactivation of the serine/threonine kinase akt/pkb;the involvement of caspase 3 in akt/pkb regulation was indicated by the ability of z-devd-fmk, a caspase 3 inhibitor, to block the alpha6beta4-associated reduction in akt/pkb levels in vivo, and by the ability of recombinant caspase 3 to promote the cleavage of akt/pkb in vitro"],"d":"list_of_string"}, {"po":49,"n":"EdgeBetweenness","v":"134.0","d":"double"},